window.HYPOTHESES = {"published_at": "2026-09-10T13:20:36.577285+00:00", "experiment": "APOE4 vs APOE3 / mock microglia", "discovery": "RNA and protein", "evaluation_features": 618, "baseline": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.5, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0, "cosine_similarity": 0.5446567723274521, "direction_accuracy": 0.8268608414239482, "hypothesis_id": "constant_positive_one", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7320097087378641, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.5, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0, "cosine_similarity": 0.5446567723274521, "direction_accuracy": 0.8268608414239482, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7320097087378641, "n_features": 618}}}, "cohorts": [{"id": "opus-original", "label": "Opus / original", "count": 996, "best": 0.5391946857970239, "mean": 0.27588171328191674, "selected_count": 2}, {"id": "sonnet-original", "label": "Sonnet / original", "count": 10, "best": 0.3101171980232298, "mean": 0.11734671255708165, "selected_count": 0}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2", "label": "Opus / evidence-v2", "count": 1325, "best": 0.5446250045637073, "mean": 0.327058261542982, "selected_count": 8}, {"id": "astra-forecast-v3", "label": "Astra / original", "count": 20, "best": 0.31591653415995535, "mean": -0.009822704097367563, "selected_count": 0}, {"id": "astra-evidence-v2", "label": "Astra / evidence-v2 / xhigh", "count": 38, "best": 0.3895856673297374, "mean": 0.15215022912407322, "selected_count": 0}, {"id": "sonnet-evidence-v2", "label": "Sonnet / evidence-v2", "count": 10, "best": 0.424771974705316, "mean": 0.28698202653700305, "selected_count": 0}, {"id": "astra-max-evidence-v2", "label": "Astra / evidence-v2 / max", "count": 99, "best": 0.46894936986598684, "mean": 0.145059269215571, "selected_count": 0}], "hypotheses": [{"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b09-hyp_165", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 9, "hypothesis": {"hypothesis_id": "hyp_165", "title": "APOE4 microglia route incoming lipid into esterified/lysosomal storage pools while ER-sensed sterol stays low, sustaining a self-reinforcing lipid-loading cell state", "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes, D30) differ from APOE3 not by an unfolded-protein-response bottleneck but by a coordinated lipid-handling cell state: transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid uptake (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:SLCO2B1, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE, gene:PLTP), for lysosomal glycohydrolases and v-ATPase (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:TFEB) and for esterification/neutral-lipid and phospholipid synthesis (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:AGPAT2, gene:LPCAT1) are all higher, yet the SREBP sterol-synthesis program is also higher (gene:SREBF2, gene:SREBF1, gene:HMGCS1, gene:ACAT2, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:SCD, gene:LDLR, gene:INSIG1), which is the signature expected when delivered sterol is routed into ester/lysosomal pools that the ER regulatory sterol sensor does not see. The predicted consequence is accumulation of cholesteryl ester, neutral lipid and lysosomal glyco/sphingolipid substrates rather than an acute degradative failure; the ER/secretory changes are read as biosynthetic support for an expanded lysosomal glycoprotein output (gene:MLEC +10.21, gene:DDOST, gene:STT3A, gene:STT3B, gene:UGGT1, gene:RPN1, gene:EMC4), not as ER stress.", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 increases the lipoprotein/lipid acquisition route of microglia: scavenger and lipid-carrier transcripts are elevated (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:SLCO2B1, gene:SCARB2, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE, gene:PLTP, gene:NPC2), together with phagocytic/opsonic receptors (gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:C1QA/B/C, gene:FCGR1A, gene:MRC1, gene:CD163).", "Increased endolysosomal lipid delivery is matched by an expanded lysosomal degradative compartment program (gene:TFEB, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:GBA2, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GLA, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, gene:SGSH, gene:MAN2B1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSH, gene:DPP7, gene:LAMP1, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:GPNMB) and by the ER-side machinery that builds these N-glycosylated hydrolases (gene:MLEC, gene:DDOST, gene:STT3A, gene:STT3B, gene:UGGT1, gene:RPN1, gene:EMC4, gene:SRP72); ambiguous 2D spots containing lysosomal hydrolase candidates are present in both directions (protein_spot:012, protein_spot:013, protein_spot:006, protein_spot:007, protein_spot:063 up; protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down), consistent with compartment remodeling but not identifying single proteins.", "Sterol and fatty acid arriving in APOE4 cells are preferentially routed into esterified and neutral-lipid/phospholipid storage rather than back to the ER-accessible regulatory sterol pool (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:AGPAT2, gene:LPCAT1, gene:FABP5, gene:MGLL, gene:ABHD5 up), while oxysterol-generating enzymes (gene:CH25H, gene:CYP27A1) and the LXR-responsive LDLR-degrading ubiquitin ligase (gene:MYLIP) are also up, indicating that a peripheral/oxysterol pool signals separately from the ER pool.", "Because the ER regulatory sterol pool is not repressed, SREBP-driven synthesis remains on and adds endogenous sterol and fatty acid to the load (gene:SREBF2, gene:SREBF1, gene:HMGCS1, gene:ACAT2, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:FADS1, gene:SCD, gene:LDLR, gene:INSIG1 all positive, 12/12, versus a 77% positive background in this selected list).", "The loop is self-reinforcing at steady state: continued uptake plus continued synthesis, with output directed to ester/droplet and lysosomal lipid pools, produces a lipid-loaded microglial state in mock conditions; degradative and biosynthetic capacity are increased, so this is a routing/cell-state change rather than a demonstrated bottleneck.", "Predicted lipid-level consequence in the same mock condition: higher cholesteryl ester and triacylglycerol, a lower free-cholesterol:cholesteryl-ester ratio, and higher lysosomal glyco/sphingolipid substrate species in APOE4 than APOE3, with reduced reserve for an additional lipid challenge revealed only if such a challenge is applied."], "assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (n=2212, all adjusted p\u003c0.05, |effect|\u003e=1.06, 77.1% positive); programs are judged against that 77% positive background, not 50/50, and unlisted genes (e.g. ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, HSPA5, XBP1, PLIN2, LIPA) are unknown, not unchanged.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified in the workbook and is preserved as reported; protein spots are log2 fold changes on a separate scale, so magnitudes are not compared across modalities.", "Transcript abundance is treated as capacity, not activity or flux: no sterol-esterification rate, SREBP2 cleavage, lysosomal hydrolytic flux, cholesterol efflux rate or lipid pool size was measured here.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate (2-6 genes each; 92 spots, 47 reported significant, 64/92 positive) and are used only for compatibility and contradiction, never as identification of a single protein.", "Program membership was fixed from canonical pathway lists before directions were inspected; all represented members, including contrary ones, are reported.", "Astrocyte co-culture means measured microglial transcripts may partly reflect a non-cell-autonomous lipid supply from astrocytes; the mechanism does not require the sterol to be microglia-derived.", "Any loss of degradative or storage reserve is a prediction for a future lipid/inflammatory challenge, not an ongoing defect claimed for the measured mock condition."], "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective lipidomics on the same mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show higher cholesteryl ester and triacylglycerol and a lower free-cholesterol:cholesteryl-ester ratio in APOE4, plus higher hexosylceramide/GM3-type lysosomal substrates; if neutral-lipid esters and lysosomal glycolipids are unchanged or lower in APOE4, the routing mechanism is weakened.", "Prospective SOAT1/ACAT inhibition (or DGAT1 inhibition) in APOE4 microglia should raise ER-accessible cholesterol and selectively suppress SREBP2 target transcripts (HMGCS1, LDLR, DHCR7, LSS) more in APOE4 than APOE3 while lowering cholesteryl ester; persistence of high SREBP2 targets after esterification blockade would falsify the 'ER pool not sensing the load' step.", "Prospective direct measurement of the ER-accessible sterol pool (e.g. ALOD4/D4H-type probe or SCAP-SREBP2 cleavage assay) should show APOE4 cells with normal-to-high total sterol but lower ER-accessible sterol and more cleaved SREBP2; equal ER-accessible sterol with equal SREBP2 processing would favor a simple increased-throughput explanation instead.", "Prospective pulse-chase with labelled lipoprotein/myelin lipid should show comparable or faster initial uptake and hydrolysis in APOE4 with a larger fraction of label retained as ester/droplet lipid and less efflux; if instead label accumulates undegraded in the lysosome with slower hydrolysis, the mechanism should be replaced by a lysosomal degradation bottleneck model.", "Prospective challenge (myelin debris or oxLDL loading) is predicted to expose reduced reserve in APOE4 (greater droplet accumulation, later induction of ER stress markers); absence of any APOE4-specific difference under challenge would argue the mock-state transcriptional differences are inconsequential for lipid handling."]}, "score": {"hypothesis_id": "hyp_165", "cosine_similarity": 0.5446250045637073, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.3521645102226441, "direction_accuracy": 0.5922330097087378, "balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.43939002326182475, "mean_absolute_error": 0.522789644012945, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"n_features": 618, "cosine_similarity": 0.5446250045637073, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.3521645102226441, "direction_accuracy": 0.5922330097087378, "balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.43939002326182475, "mean_absolute_error": 0.522789644012945}}}, "cost_usd": 1.69600975, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 1, "global_rank": 1}, {"id": "opus-original-b07-hyp_189", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 7, "hypothesis": {"hypothesis_id": "hyp_189", "title": "APOE4 microglia amplify lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase transcription while relatively downgrading late-fusion SNAREs, making cargo delivery into the lysosome the catabolic bottleneck", "claim": "In isogenic mock-treated iPSC-derived microglia, the APOE4 genotype is associated with a coordinated transcript increase in acid hydrolases, v-ATPase subunits and TFEB together with a relative decrease in the SNARE machinery that executes late-endosome/autophagosome-to-lysosome fusion (STX17, STX16, VAMP2, STXBP5). We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step in APOE4 microglia is delivery of internalised and autophagic lipid cargo into the acidified hydrolase-rich compartment, not hydrolase supply or particle uptake, so lipid substrate dwells upstream of the lysosome while SREBP-linked lipogenic transcripts remain high; uptake and phagocytic-receptor machinery is not reduced, so this is a post-internalisation handling defect rather than a phagocytic-cup/actin defect.", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 cells show a coherent above-background elevation of lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts (GAA, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, ATP6V1A, ATP6V1H) plus TFEB; we infer, but did not measure, increased lysosomal biogenesis drive and hydrolase protein synthesis.", "In the same comparison, transcripts encoding the fusion step that delivers late endosomes/autophagosomes to lysosomes (STX17, STX16, VAMP2, STXBP5) fall in the lowest ~13% of this differential-expression list, while recycling-route SNAREs (VAMP3, STX12) do not; we infer a relative shift of membrane traffic away from degradative fusion toward recycling.", "The proposed bottleneck is therefore the fusion/delivery step: catabolic flux through the lysosome is limited by cargo access to hydrolases rather than by hydrolase abundance (flux, localisation and fusion rate are inferred, not measured here).", "Internalised lipid-rich cargo and autophagic membrane consequently dwell in pre-lysosomal compartments and neutral-lipid stores; sterol liberated from such cargo does not reach the ER sensing pool, so SREBP-linked lipogenic/sterol transcripts (SREBF1, SREBF2, INSIG1, SCD, DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS, DGAT1) stay high and add further lipid load.", "Hydrolase output that cannot engage cargo is predicted to redistribute between proform, mature and secreted pools; 2-D protein spots whose candidate lists include CTSB or CTSD change in opposite directions (spots 055/057/053 up, 058/067/069 down), which is consistent with, but does not identify, such redistribution.", "Because phagocytic-receptor and ARP2/3 transcripts (TREM2, MERTK, SCARB1, ITGB1, ITGAX, C1QA-C, ARPC1B, ARPC4, ARPC5) are not reduced relative to the global shift, the net APOE4 phenotype is predicted to be normal-or-increased uptake with slowed post-uptake degradation and lipid retention."], "assumptions": ["The RNA effects are reported log fold changes of unspecified base from a pre-selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e 1), so only ranks relative to the strong global positive shift (median +1.46) are interpreted, not absolute magnitudes.", "Transcript changes for SNARE and hydrolase genes are assumed to track the corresponding protein and complex abundance; neither protein was measured for STX17, STX16, VAMP2 or STXBP5 in the supplied data.", "Protein spots have multiple candidate genes and are treated as ambiguous, non-identifying evidence only.", "Lysosomal pH, fusion rate, cargo flux, lipid droplet content and cholesteryl esters were not measured; all flux, localisation and causal statements are inferred.", "Astrocyte co-culture and the 10X Flex pseudobulk-style comparison with unstated replicate number could contribute composition effects that the supplied data cannot exclude; causality is not established."], "falsifiable_predictions": ["Pulse-chase with fluorescent myelin or pHrodo/DQ-BSA cargo: APOE4 microglia should internalise at least as much as APOE3 at early times (\u003c=30 min) but show reduced cargo-LAMP1 colocalisation and slower DQ-BSA dequenching later; if APOE4 instead internalises less at early times, the uptake/actin-cytoskeleton alternative is supported and this mechanism is weakened.", "Restoring STX17 (and/or STX16) expression in APOE4 microglia should increase cargo-lysosome fusion and lower BODIPY neutral-lipid load without raising hydrolase transcripts; no reduction in lipid load despite verified restoration would weaken the mechanism.", "Knockdown of STX17 in APOE3 microglia should phenocopy APOE4 lipid retention and slowed cargo degradation; failure to phenocopy weakens the bottleneck assignment.", "SREBP or SCD inhibition should reduce droplet load but should NOT normalise cargo-to-lysosome delivery kinetics; if it normalises delivery, lipogenic supply rather than fusion is the primary bottleneck.", "Immunoblot/immunostain in APOE4 versus APOE3 should show reduced STX17 and STX16 protein with unchanged or increased mature CTSB/CTSD and v-ATPase subunits; unchanged STX17/STX16 protein, or reduced mature cathepsins, would weaken the core premise.", "Bafilomycin A1 or hydrolase inhibition should increase lipid retention proportionally less in APOE4 than in APOE3, because APOE4 degradative flux is already delivery-limited; an equal or larger APOE4 response would weaken the mechanism."]}, "score": {"hypothesis_id": "hyp_189", "cosine_similarity": 0.5391946857970239, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23482078475066162, "direction_accuracy": 0.6148867313915858, "balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.37084148727984345, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5231197411003237, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"n_features": 618, "cosine_similarity": 0.5391946857970239, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23482078475066162, "direction_accuracy": 0.6148867313915858, "balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.37084148727984345, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5231197411003237}}}, "cost_usd": 1.80450075, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 1, "global_rank": 2}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b10-hyp_026", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 10, "hypothesis": {"hypothesis_id": "hyp_026", "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a lipid-acquisition-and-storage cell state with coupled lysosomal and mitochondrial-anabolic expansion, not an interferon/inflammatory state", "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-derived microglia (APOE4 vs APOE3, day 30, astrocyte co-culture), the dominant difference in the supplied selected differential-expression list is a coordinated lipid-handling cell state: sterol/fatty-acid synthesis, esterification and lipid-uptake-receptor transcripts are uniformly higher in APOE4 (24/24 represented members positive) together with a TFEB-associated lysosomal/autophagy transcript program (25/26 positive) and a mitochondrial carrier/TCA/OXPHOS program (22/22 positive), whereas interferon-stimulated genes are essentially unrepresented and NF-kB/chemokine members are indistinguishable from the strongly up-biased selected-list background. We propose that APOE4-associated poor lipid off-loading routes acquired lipid into esterified and endolysosomal storage pools so that the ER-accessible regulatory sterol pool stays low; SREBP-responsive synthesis and uptake transcripts therefore remain elevated instead of being repressed, and the enlarged cargo load is matched by lysosomal-catabolic and mitochondrial anaplerotic transcript expansion. This is an altered-routing/coordinated-state change measurable as transcript abundance; whether clearance flux is adequate (successful adaptation) or already saturating (failed compensation) is not determined by these data.", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 protein is a poorer lipid acceptor/donor than APOE3 (background knowledge, not measured here), so cholesterol and phospholipid leaving microglia on APOE particles is reduced in the co-culture; APOE transcript itself is modestly higher in APOE4 (gene:APOE +1.2), i.e. the difference is not simply less APOE message.", "Acquired lipid is routed into esterified/neutral-lipid and endolysosomal storage rather than export: esterification and triacylglycerol/desaturation transcripts (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:AGPAT2, gene:AGPAT4, gene:SCD, gene:FABP5) and lipid/lipoprotein uptake receptor transcripts (gene:SCARB1 +8.2, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK, gene:MRC1) are all higher in APOE4.", "Because sterol accumulates in storage and lysosomal compartments rather than in the ER-accessible regulatory pool, SREBP-responsive transcripts remain on instead of being repressed: gene:SREBF1 +4.7, gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP. Co-elevation of uptake plus de novo synthesis plus esterification is the signature that distinguishes mis-sensing/routing from a lipid-replete state, in which synthesis and LDLR transcripts should fall.", "The increased lysosomal cargo load coincides with a TFEB-associated lysosomal-catabolic and autophagy transcript expansion (gene:TFEB, gene:GAA +10.0, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:RAB7A, gene:ATG4A, gene:ATG4D, gene:ATG9A), i.e. capacity is being built, not simply lost.", "Mitochondrial carrier, TCA and OXPHOS transcripts rise in parallel (gene:SLC25A1 citrate carrier, gene:MPC2, gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:ACO2, gene:DLD, gene:ACSS2, gene:NDUFA5, gene:ATP5ME, gene:SLC25A46), consistent with supplying citrate/acetyl-CoA and reducing equivalents for the elevated esterification and membrane-biogenesis load, alongside higher translation-initiation transcripts (gene:EIF2A, gene:EIF4E, gene:EIF3L, gene:EIF4G3).", "Net predicted state in the actual mock condition: APOE4 microglia hold more esterified/neutral lipid and a larger acidic compartment while continuing to import and synthesise lipid; reduced clearance reserve, if present, would be revealed only by a lipid or myelin/apoptotic-cargo challenge and is not established by these measurements."], "assumptions": ["RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, all |effect| \u003e= 1, 77% positive) in an unspecified logarithm base; effects are treated as ordinal and programs are compared against this up-biased selected background, not a 50/50 expectation. Genes absent from the list are unknown, not unchanged (e.g. NPC1, ABCA1, ABCG1, LIPA, PLIN2, STAT1, ISG15, IL1B, TNF are simply not supplied).", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for pathway state; SREBP-2/SREBP-1 cleavage, TFEB nuclear localisation, mTORC1 activity, lysosomal pH, hydrolase catalytic activity, lipid flux and APOE secretion were not measured and are inferred, not observed.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel features with 2-6 candidate identities each (208 candidate genes across 92 spots, keratin/actin dominating); no spot is assigned to a single protein, and the spot set shows a mild global positive shift (median about +0.5 log2), so spots are used only for compatibility/contradiction, not confirmation.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 in astrocyte co-culture, so part of the microglial lipid state may be non-cell-autonomous (astrocyte-derived lipoproteins); the mechanism does not require the routing defect to be purely microglia-intrinsic.", "Descriptive program coherence and the permutation comparisons used here treat genes as independent, which they are not; no formal enrichment claim is made.", "Causality is not established by these observational abundance differences; the proposed routing step is a hypothesis to be tested, and any clearance-reserve deficit is a challenge-revealed prediction rather than an observed defect under mock."], "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective imaging/lipidomics in the same mock condition: APOE4 microglia should contain more neutral-lipid droplets (BODIPY 493/503) and more cholesteryl ester, plus larger LAMP1/LysoTracker volume, than isogenic APOE3. If CE and neutral-lipid content are equal or lower in APOE4 despite the elevated synthesis/uptake/esterification transcripts, the storage-routing step is wrong and the state is better described as increased throughput.", "Discriminating sterol-repletion test: acute loading with cholesterol:methyl-beta-cyclodextrin or with APOE3-containing lipoprotein particles should repress SREBP-target transcripts (LDLR, HMGCS1, DHCR24, SREBF1) and SCARB1/CD36 substantially more in APOE4 than in APOE3, because APOE4 cells are predicted to start with a low ER-accessible regulatory sterol pool. If APOE4 and APOE3 repress these genes equally, or APOE4 fails to repress at all (sensing-independent), the proposed mis-routing/mis-sensing step is weakened in favour of a growth/biogenesis-driven anabolic state.", "SOAT1/ACAT inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) or DGAT1 inhibition should lower esterified stores and, if routing is correct, partially normalise SREBP-target and lysosomal transcripts in APOE4 toward APOE3. Persistence of the transcript differences with reduced esters, or overt free-cholesterol toxicity, would argue that storage is a protective adaptation downstream of a different primary lesion.", "Flux versus capacity test: DQ-BSA and fluorescent myelin/apoptotic-cargo pulse-chase should show APOE4 degrading basal cargo at a rate at least equal to APOE3 (consistent with adaptation matching the transcript expansion) while saturating earlier at high cargo load. Finding lower basal degradation rate in APOE4 despite higher hydrolase transcripts would replace this hypothesis with a failed-compensation variant in which lysosomal transcript induction is a response to an already-defective clearance step.", "Negative/specificity prediction: JAK1/2 inhibition or IFNAR1 blockade should not normalise the lipid, lysosomal or mitochondrial transcript differences between APOE4 and APOE3 under mock, consistent with interferon signalling being unrepresented here (only IFI27L2, IFI16, IRF8, IRF5 present; IRF2 negative; no STAT1/ISG15/MX/OAS/IFIT rows supplied). If JAK inhibition abolishes the lipid-program difference, the interferon-driven alternative is favoured over this mechanism."]}, "score": {"hypothesis_id": "hyp_026", "cosine_similarity": 0.5286248382495118, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.28619861379973505, "direction_accuracy": 0.5566343042071198, "balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3356164383561644, "mean_absolute_error": 0.4979870550161813, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"n_features": 618, "cosine_similarity": 0.5286248382495118, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.28619861379973505, "direction_accuracy": 0.5566343042071198, "balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3356164383561644, "mean_absolute_error": 0.4979870550161813}}}, "cost_usd": 2.008293, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 2, "global_rank": 3}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_073", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"hypothesis_id": "hyp_073", "title": "APOE4 microglia bias carbon into a mitochondrial TCA/citrate-export node that feeds SREBF1-driven neutral-lipid esterification, with lysosomal hydrolase transcription rising only as a secondary response", "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by a coherent transcriptional expansion of mitochondrial pyruvate/anaplerotic entry, TCA-cycle enzymes and mitochondrial carriers that outstrips the global upward shift of this differential-expression list, while glycolytic commitment steps are not co-induced. We propose the rate-limiting node is mitochondrial citrate/malate export (SLC25A1-SLC25A11 exchange), which supplies cytosolic acetyl-CoA for an SREBF1-associated lipogenic and sterol-esterification program (SCD, DGAT1, SOAT1, ACAT2, DHCR24), producing neutral-lipid accumulation. Increased lysosomal hydrolase and V-ATPase mRNA (including TFEB) is interpreted as a downstream CLEAR-type response to lipid load rather than the primary defect, because it is weaker than the mitochondrial signal, internally discordant (CTSS, IDS decreased) and not corroborated at the protein-spot level. Causality is not established by these data.", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia show higher mRNA for mitochondrial substrate entry and anaplerosis (MPC2, GLUD1, GLS, NNT). We infer, but did not measure, increased pyruvate and glutamate-derived carbon entry into the matrix.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): TCA-cycle enzyme transcripts (ACO2, OGDH, DLD, IDH3G, MDH1, GOT1) are coordinately elevated well above the list-wide shift, implying increased citrate/malate cycling capacity; enzyme activity and metabolite pools were not measured.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred flux partitioning): electron-transport subunit transcripts (NDUFA5, NDUFS7, UQCRC2, COX7A2, ATP5ME and ~35 further subunits) rise while committed glycolytic steps do not (HK2 and PFKP decreased), consistent with an oxidative rather than glycolytic bias; oxygen consumption was not measured.", "Step 4 (proposed bottleneck, measured RNA only): the exit of carbon from the matrix as citrate via SLC25A1, balanced by SLC25A11 malate/2-oxoglutarate exchange and SLC25A5 adenine-nucleotide exchange, is the step we propose limits how much of this oxidative carbon is diverted to cytosolic acetyl-CoA; ACSS2 provides a parallel acetate-derived route. Cytosolic acetyl-CoA and citrate pools are unmeasured and must not be treated as observed.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred activity): the cytosolic acetyl-CoA supply supports an SREBF1-associated program (SCD, DGAT1, ACAT2, SOAT1, DHCR24, INSIG1, LDLR, MYLIP), which we infer channels fatty acid and sterol into triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester; SREBP processing, localization and lipid species were not measured.", "Step 6 (secondary, partly discordant): the resulting neutral-lipid and membrane load engages a CLEAR-type transcriptional response (TFEB up; GAA, CTSB, CTSD, and V-ATPase subunit mRNA up), which we treat as compensatory rather than causal because cathepsin- and V-ATPase-containing protein spots move in both directions and CTSS and IDS mRNA are decreased."], "assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (every |effect| exceeds 1) with a strong list-wide positive shift, so only within-list rank enrichment, not absolute direction, is interpreted; the logarithm base and pseudocount are unspecified and effects are treated as ordinal.", "Coordinated transcript increases in a nuclear-encoded TCA/ETC/carrier module reflect increased pathway capacity rather than a normalization, ambient-RNA or cell-quality artifact that preferentially inflates highly expressed housekeeping transcripts.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for enzyme abundance and for flux at steps where no protein, metabolite, flux or localization measurement is supplied (all of Steps 1-5).", "Protein spots contain 3-6 candidate genes each and show frequent keratin and actin contamination, so no spot is assigned to a unique protein; spots are used only as weak, non-identifying corroboration or counter-evidence.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype-driven astrocyte lipid or APOE secretion could contribute to the microglial state; cell-type deconvolution and any lipid, oxygen-consumption or tracer measurement are absent from the supplied data.", "SREBF1 target induction is assumed to reflect increased SREBP-1 transcriptional activity rather than only compensatory feedback to sterol depletion."], "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: in APOE4 microglia, SLC25A1 knockdown or citrate-carrier inhibition (CTPI-2) should lower neutral-lipid droplet content and de novo 13C-glucose incorporation into C16:0/C18:1 toward APOE3 levels, while leaving ETC subunit transcript elevation largely intact. If LD content and glucose-derived fatty-acid labelling are unchanged by SLC25A1 loss, the proposed citrate-export bottleneck is wrong.", "13C-glucose and 13C-glutamine tracing should show higher M+2 citrate enrichment and a higher glucose-derived fraction of cytosolic fatty acid in APOE4 than APOE3 under mock. Equal or lower enrichment in APOE4 would weaken Steps 1-4.", "Extracellular flux analysis should show higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption in APOE4 without a matched increase in glycolytic rate. A glycolytic rather than oxidative shift, or no OCR difference, would weaken Step 3.", "Discriminating against the lysosomal-capacity alternative: acute lysosomal inhibition (bafilomycin A1 or a pan-cathepsin inhibitor) should increase lipid droplets in both genotypes but should not abolish the APOE4-over-APOE3 excess, whereas DGAT1 or SCD inhibition should collapse that excess. If the APOE4 excess disappears only with lysosomal manipulation, the primary bottleneck is endolysosomal, not the citrate-export node.", "Bulk cathepsin B/D and beta-glucocerebrosidase enzymatic activity and mature-cathepsin immunoblots should not be uniformly higher in APOE4 despite elevated transcripts, matching the bidirectional cathepsin-containing spots. Uniformly higher hydrolase activity plus intact substrate clearance would argue the CLEAR response is sufficient and would weaken Step 6.", "TFEB nuclear translocation should be a consequence of lipid load: pharmacological blockade of neutral-lipid esterification should reduce TFEB target transcripts in APOE4. Persistent TFEB target induction after lipid-storage blockade would place the lysosomal program upstream and falsify the ordering in Step 6."]}, "score": {"hypothesis_id": "hyp_073", "cosine_similarity": 0.5279950098961133, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.302168459557284, "direction_accuracy": 0.5, "balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3013698630136986, "mean_absolute_error": 0.512948220064725, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"n_features": 618, "cosine_similarity": 0.5279950098961133, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.302168459557284, "direction_accuracy": 0.5, "balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3013698630136986, "mean_absolute_error": 0.512948220064725}}}, "cost_usd": 1.883722, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 2, "global_rank": 4}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b08-hyp_158", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 8, "hypothesis": {"hypothesis_id": "hyp_158", "title": "APOE4 microglia install an expanded uptake-to-lysosome degradative and oxidative state whose late fusion/retrograde export step is not scaled, leaving ER sterol sensing unsatisfied", "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes, day 30) differ from APOE3 not by a single enzyme defect but by a coordinated cell-state change: transcripts for lipoprotein/phagocytic uptake receptors, for CLEAR-type lysosomal hydrolases (including the sphingolipid hydrolases SMPD1, GBA, HEXA/HEXB, GM2A, GLA) and V-ATPase subunits, for retromer/ESCRT sorting, and for nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits are coordinately higher, while transcripts for the late fusion/retrograde-export step (STX17, STX16, VAMP2, STXBP5, BET1L, M6PR, RAB27A) and mtDNA-encoded transcripts are lower than the strongly up-shifted background of this selected DE list. We propose that increased cargo influx into an enlarged, acidification- and hydrolase-rich endolysosomal compartment, combined with a non-scaled fusion/retrograde export step, keeps the ER-accessible sterol pool from being replenished, so SREBP-driven synthesis/uptake output (SREBF1/2, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, EBP, ACAT2, SCD, INSIG1, LDLR) stays on together with esterification/storage and efflux gene output (SOAT1, DGAT1, AGPAT2, LPCAT1, ABCA7, APOE), and the maintenance cost is answered by nuclear OXPHOS induction. This is a directional inference from measured transcript abundance and ambiguous protein spots; no flux, lipid pool, localization or causality was measured.", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured transcripts, inferred influx): APOE4 microglia express higher lipoprotein/phagocytic receptor transcripts (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:MRC1, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:TREM2, gene:C1QA/B/C, gene:FCGR1A/1B/3A, gene:SIRPA, gene:LDLR; 19/19 represented members positive vs a 77% positive list background), which we infer increases internalization of lipid-rich cargo.", "Step 2 (measured, inferred capacity): Cargo enters an expanded endolysosomal compartment - CLEAR-type transcription factors (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF) and unusually large increases in hydrolase and V-ATPase transcripts (gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD, gene:GM2A, gene:GLA, gene:GBA2, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:LAMP1) plus retromer/ESCRT/Rab sorting genes (gene:VPS26A, gene:VPS35L, gene:SNX3, gene:CHMP4B, gene:VPS37B, gene:RAB7A) - i.e. increased degradative and acidification capacity, not a hydrolase deficiency.", "Step 3 (measured deficit, inferred routing limit): Against this up-shifted background, the late fusion/retrograde and export machinery is selectively low (gene:STX17 -2.06, gene:STX16 -4.06, gene:VAMP2 -1.85, gene:STXBP5 -5.52, gene:BET1L -3.80, gene:STXBP2 -1.21, gene:M6PR -1.72, gene:RAB27A -2.52, gene:CTSS -5.57, gene:VPS13B -4.65, gene:OSBPL8 -1.90; 2/8 SNARE-module members positive, binomial p=0.003 vs the 77% background), which we infer limits the hand-off of degraded lipid back to ER/Golgi and to secretory/export routes rather than limiting degradation itself.", "Step 4 (inferred sensing consequence): Because the ER-accessible sterol pool is not replenished, SREBP output remains on despite high uptake-receptor expression (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:ACAT2, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR; 13/13 represented members positive), while carbon is diverted into esters/membrane storage and efflux (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:LPCAT1, gene:MBOAT1/2, gene:ABCA7, gene:APOE, gene:CH25H, gene:CYP27A1, gene:SCP2 +5.95, gene:NPC2).", "Step 5 (inferred cost): Sustaining influx, acidification (V-ATPase), lysosome biogenesis and lipid resynthesis raises ATP/redox demand, matching the strongest single pattern in the data - coordinate induction of nuclear-encoded OXPHOS/TCA transcripts (38/38 represented members positive, binomial p\u003c1e-4; gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:NDUFS7, gene:NDUFS8, gene:UQCRC2, gene:ATP5ME, gene:COX7A2, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56) together with peroxiredoxins (gene:PRDX2, gene:PRDX3, gene:GPX4); mtDNA-encoded transcripts are not co-induced (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-CO2, gene:MT-ND4), so the increase in assembled respiratory capacity is inferred to be incomplete.", "Step 6 (downstream state): This chronically engaged clearance state accompanies modest innate-immune priming without a full interferon program (gene:MYD88, gene:TLR2, gene:TLR6, gene:TICAM1, gene:SYK, gene:NLRP3, gene:PYCARD, gene:IL18, gene:CXCL8, gene:CXCL16, gene:CCL2, gene:A2M), which we interpret as a consequence of prolonged lysosomal lipid handling rather than an independent activating stimulus."], "assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all adjusted p\u003c0.05, |effect|\u003e=1, 77% positive, unspecified logarithm base); program directions were judged against that 77%-positive background, and genes absent from the list (e.g. SPTLC1/2, SGMS1/2, UGCG, NPC1, LIPA, PSAP, STX7, VAMP7/8, SNAP29) are unknown, not unchanged.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, with unmeasured delay and efficiency, the abundance of the corresponding proteins and thus compartment capacity; this assumption is only weakly testable here and is partly contradicted by the protein spots (see below).", "Protein spots are ambiguous: each carries 2-6 candidate identities and many contain actin/keratin, so spots containing CTSD/CTSB/CTSL/HEXB/GNS/ATP6V1E1 candidates (protein_spot:027, 052, 053, 055, 057 up; protein_spot:058, 064, 065, 067, 069 down) are used only as compatibility/contradiction tests and are not read as confirmation of any individual protein.", "No lipid species, cholesterol pool, hydrolase activity, autophagic or endosomal flux, respiration rate, localization or protein maturation state was measured; all statements about routing, sequestration, sensing and flux are inferences, not observations, and causal direction is not established.", "Effects expected in the supplied mock condition: the transcriptional state itself (uptake, CLEAR, sterol-synthesis, OXPHOS, low fusion-machinery). Effects expected only under future challenge: any frank clearance failure, respiratory-reserve deficit, or lipid-overload toxicity. A reduced reserve under challenge would not establish an ongoing defect in mock.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies exogenous lipoproteins/lipid cargo; if the cultures were lipid-poor, the influx premise of Step 1 fails.", "The mtDNA-encoded decrease is assumed to be biological rather than an ambient-RNA or 10X Flex probe-set artefact; only 6 MT rows are present."], "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective lipid-routing test: pulse-chase APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia with labelled lipoprotein/myelin/apoptotic cargo. Predicted: equal or higher internalization in APOE4, longer residence in LAMP1+ compartments, higher cholesteryl-ester/neutral-lipid content, and lower ER-accessible cholesterol (ALOD4/D4H probe) with elevated nuclear SREBP-2. If APOE4 shows equal or faster cargo clearance and equal or higher ER-accessible cholesterol while SREBP targets are still elevated, the routing-limited mechanism is wrong and the 'membrane demand for successful compartment expansion' alternative is favoured.", "Prospective fusion-step rescue: re-expressing STX17 (and separately VAMP2 or STX16) in APOE4 microglia should accelerate autophagosome/late-endosome-lysosome fusion and lower SREBP target transcripts and cholesteryl esters toward APOE3 levels without lowering hydrolase transcripts. No change in either flux or sterol-synthesis output would weaken Step 3-4.", "Prospective sphingolipid test of the assigned focus: measure sphingolipid species and hydrolase activities. The mechanism (hydrolase induction secondary to load) predicts that despite higher SMPD1/GBA/HEXA/HEXB/GM2A transcripts, glucosylceramide, GM2/GM3 and sphingomyelin will be equal or higher in APOE4, not lower. Finding reduced sphingolipid substrates with proportionally increased ceramide/S1P output would instead indicate successful increased catabolic throughput and would demote this mechanism to a sphingolipid-turnover-gain model.", "Prospective bioenergetic test: Seahorse/BN-PAGE on mock cells. Predicted: basal respiration modestly higher in APOE4 but assembled complex I/III/IV and maximal (FCCP) respiration not increased in proportion to the 38/38 nuclear-subunit transcript increase, reflecting the uncoupled mtDNA-encoded transcripts. Full proportional scaling of maximal respiration would weaken Step 5 (and would not by itself refute Steps 1-4).", "Prospective causality control: acutely blocking cargo influx (anti-SCARB1/CD36 blockade or lipoprotein-depleted medium) in APOE4 should, within 24-48 h, reduce CLEAR/hydrolase and OXPHOS transcript elevation. Persistence of the whole program under cargo withdrawal would indicate a genotype-intrinsic transcriptional state upstream of lipid load and would refute the load-driven ordering of the mechanism."]}, "score": {"hypothesis_id": "hyp_158", "cosine_similarity": 0.5268673891755167, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23835462848449185, "direction_accuracy": 0.6245954692556634, "balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3776908023483366, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5139967637540452, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"n_features": 618, "cosine_similarity": 0.5268673891755167, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23835462848449185, "direction_accuracy": 0.6245954692556634, "balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3776908023483366, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5139967637540452}}}, "cost_usd": 2.430692, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 3, "global_rank": 5}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b08-hyp_012", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 8, "hypothesis": {"hypothesis_id": "hyp_012", "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a cargo-avid lipid-processing state: receptor-mediated uptake and lysosomal expansion feed mitochondrial oxidative disposal while sterol is routed to esters, so SREBP-driven acquisition stays on", "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes) differ from APOE3 chiefly by a coordinated cell-state shift toward lipid/debris acquisition and lysosomal-oxidative processing, not by a single enzymatic block: uptake and phagocytic-receptor transcripts (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:FCGR1A/3A/FCGRT, gene:ITGB1, gene:ITGA6, gene:C1QA/B/C, 22/22 represented members positive), lysosomal biogenesis transcripts (gene:TFEB, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:GAA, gene:ATP6V1H and other v-ATPase subunits; 26/28 positive), nuclear-encoded OXPHOS and TCA/carrier transcripts (38/38 and 14/14 positive, e.g. gene:NDUFA5, gene:ATP5ME, gene:UQCRC2, gene:MPC2, gene:OGDH, gene:MDH1, gene:HADHA, gene:ETFA) are jointly elevated above the strongly up-biased selected-list background (77.1% of 2212 DE rows positive), while glycolytic commitment genes are mixed-to-down (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:TALDO1 -2.32). Within this state, sterol handling shows a distinctive internal inconsistency: acquisition and storage genes rise together with sterol-anabolic genes (gene:LDLR, gene:SREBF2, gene:SREBF1, gene:HMGCS1, gene:ACAT2, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:INSIG1, all positive, 10/10 represented mevalonate/SREBP-2 members) alongside esterification/storage and lysosomal-sterol genes (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SCP2, gene:NPC2, gene:CH25H, gene:CYP27A1), which is the pattern expected when incoming sterol is diverted into cholesteryl-ester/lysosomal pools rather than the ER-accessible pool that terminates SREBP-2 output. We claim increased throughput with an unsatisfied ER sterol set-point, not a demonstrated rate-limiting defect.", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured transcript state, inferred function): APOE4 microglia up-regulate receptor systems for lipoprotein, lipid and debris cargo (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:FCGR1A, gene:FCGR3A, gene:FCGRT, gene:ITGB1, gene:ITGA6, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:C1QA/C1QB/C1QC, gene:SYK), which we infer raises delivery of lipid-rich cargo into the endolysosomal system; the flux itself is not measured.", "Step 2: Increased cargo load is matched by a TFEB-associated expansion of degradative capacity (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF, gene:ATP6V1A/ATP6V1H/ATP6V0C and other v-ATPase subunits, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA/HEXB, gene:SMPD1, gene:GAA, gene:NAGLU, gene:LAMP1), i.e. adaptation of the lysosome to lipid catabolism rather than lysosomal failure.", "Step 3: Lipid-derived acyl-CoA/acetyl-CoA is preferentially disposed of oxidatively: nuclear-encoded respiratory chain, TCA and mitochondrial carrier transcripts rise coherently (gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:UQCRC2, gene:ATP5ME, gene:COX7A2, gene:MPC2, gene:OGDH, gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1, gene:SLC25A1, gene:SLC25A11, gene:HADHA, gene:ETFA, gene:ACOX1, gene:CROT) while glycolytic/PPP commitment genes fall (gene:HK2, gene:PFKP, gene:PGD, gene:TALDO1); this is a routing change in fuel use, inferred from transcripts only.", "Step 4: Free cholesterol released from cargo is re-esterified and stored, and part is oxidized/exported as oxysterol rather than reaching the ER sensing pool (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SCP2, gene:FABP5, gene:CIDEB, gene:ABHD5, gene:CH25H, gene:CYP27A1, gene:NPC2), so ER-accessible sterol stays low relative to total cell sterol.", "Step 5: Because the ER sterol set-point is not satisfied, SREBP-driven acquisition and synthesis output remains on rather than being switched off by the lipid load (gene:LDLR, gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1, gene:HMGCS1, gene:ACAT2, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, plus SREBP-1/fatty-acid arm gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:ACSS2, gene:FADS1, gene:AGPAT2, gene:GPAT4).", "Step 6: The combination (continued acquisition + continued synthesis + esterification/storage) is self-reinforcing and predicts progressive neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester accumulation and an inflammatory-tilted, oxidative microglial state (gene:CXCL8, gene:CXCL16, gene:CXCL2, gene:CCL2, gene:IL18, gene:NLRP3, gene:ITGAX, gene:CLEC7A, gene:GPNMB, gene:APOE) that is sustainable at mock baseline but has reduced reserve if cargo or oxidative demand increases."], "assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1.0, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 2212 rows, 77.1% positive); program coherence was judged against that up-biased background, not against 50/50. Absent genes (e.g. ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, HMGCR, SQLE, IDI1, LIPA, P2RY12) are unknown, not unchanged, so neither an efflux block nor upper-mevalonate induction is claimed.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified ('reported log fold change'); effects are used as directions and relative sizes only, and the very large magnitudes (up to 15.5) are treated as noisy single-cell estimates.", "Transcript abundance is treated as capacity/state, not activity or flux: no sterol pool, cholesteryl-ester content, SREBP-2 cleavage, lysosomal pH, phagocytic rate or respiration was measured here.", "The 92 protein spots are 2-6-candidate ambiguous identifications (KRT1/KRT10/ACTB dominate the candidate lists); they are used only for compatibility, never to confirm an individual protein. Cathepsin-containing spots go both ways (protein_spot:052/053/055/057/027 up; protein_spot:058/067/069 down), so the lysosomal protein layer is unresolved.", "Genes within a program are not independent (shared regulation, shared read pileups), so the sign-coherence statistics quoted in analysis.md are descriptive, not formal enrichment tests.", "Astrocyte co-culture is assumed to supply the extracellular lipoprotein/lipid cargo that the uptake step requires; genotype effects on astrocyte-derived cargo are not measured and could drive part of the microglial state.", "Steps 1-5 are proposed for the actual mock condition; the reduced-reserve element of step 6 is a prediction about a future challenge, not an observed defect at baseline."], "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective sterol-feedback test: loading APOE4 and APOE3 microglia with LDL or 25-hydroxycholesterol will suppress SREBP-2 target transcripts (gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:DHCR7, gene:INSIG1) and nuclear SREBP-2 cleavage less in APOE4 than APOE3. Equal suppression in both genotypes would falsify the unsatisfied-ER-sterol-set-point element (step 5) and favor a generic anabolic/activated state.", "Prospective storage test: APOE4 microglia will contain more esterified cholesterol/neutral-lipid droplets than APOE3 at mock baseline, and SOAT1 inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) will raise ER-accessible free cholesterol and lower LDLR/HMGCS1 transcripts more in APOE4 than APOE3. No genotype difference in ester content, or no genotype-selective response to SOAT1 inhibition, would weaken step 4.", "Prospective cargo-dependence test: reducing cargo delivery (SCARB1/CD36 blockade, or lipoprotein/debris-depleted medium) will blunt the APOE4 elevation of lysosomal (gene:CTSB, gene:GBA, gene:ATP6V1H) and OXPHOS/TCA (gene:NDUFA5, gene:MPC2) transcripts. Persistence of these programs when uptake is blocked would falsify the proposed ordering (steps 1-3) and support a cell-autonomous transcriptional-state driver instead.", "Prospective flux test: respirometry will show higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption and greater etomoxir/fatty-acid-oxidation dependence in APOE4 than APOE3 under mock conditions, with lower glycolytic reliance. Equal or lower APOE4 respiration despite the 38/38 positive nuclear OXPHOS transcripts would indicate assembly/translation limitation (consistent with the discordant gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4 decreases) and would replace 'increased oxidative throughput' with 'failed mitochondrial compensation'.", "Prospective challenge test: on myelin-debris or apoptotic-cell loading, APOE4 microglia will show earlier lysosomal lipid accumulation and a larger inflammatory increment (gene:CXCL8, gene:IL18, gene:NLRP3) than APOE3, revealing reduced reserve. Identical challenge kinetics would indicate the mock-state differences are a benign adaptive set-point shift, not a reduced-reserve state."]}, "score": {"hypothesis_id": "hyp_012", "cosine_similarity": 0.5251993556156962, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25584450751905585, "direction_accuracy": 0.5922330097087378, "balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.35812133072407043, "mean_absolute_error": 0.49934951456310683, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"n_features": 618, "cosine_similarity": 0.5251993556156962, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25584450751905585, "direction_accuracy": 0.5922330097087378, "balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.35812133072407043, "mean_absolute_error": 0.49934951456310683}}}, "cost_usd": 2.040235, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 4, "global_rank": 6}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b09-hyp_041", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 9, "hypothesis": {"hypothesis_id": "hyp_041", "title": "APOE4 microglia run a feed-forward lipid-routing circuit: expanded endolysosomal uptake/degradation compartment plus SREBP-driven synthesis and SOAT1/DGAT1 esterification, with ER-accessible sterol sensing still reading 'low'", "claim": "In mock-treated day-30 iPSC-derived microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, the APOE4 genotype is distinguished not by a single failed enzyme but by a coordinated re-routing of lipid: transcripts for lipid-cargo receptors and endosome-to-lysosome trafficking are higher, the TFEB/MITF-type lysosomal-hydrolase and v-ATPase program is higher, and, despite this increased input, the sterol-responsive biosynthetic program (SREBP-2/SREBP-1 targets) is also higher together with esterification/storage enzymes (SOAT1, DGAT1). The most parsimonious reading is that acquired and newly made lipid is routed into lysosomal and esterified (droplet) pools rather than into the ER-accessible regulatory sterol pool, so sterol sensing continues to call for synthesis and uptake and the loop feeds forward. This predicts higher stored neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester and lysosomal glycosphingolipid content in APOE4 under mock, but it does NOT establish a degradative bottleneck: hydrolase transcripts are up, not down, and no flux, activity, localization, or free-versus-esterified pool was measured.", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured transcripts, inferred routing): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein-cargo receptors and scavenging (gene:SCARB1 +8.2, gene:CD36 +1.4, gene:LDLR +1.5, gene:MRC1 +1.4, gene:STAB1 +1.1) and for internalization and endosome-to-lysosome delivery machinery (gene:DNM2 +5.8, gene:VPS26A +4.9, gene:SNX3 +3.9, gene:CHMP4B +3.8, gene:RAB7A +2.7, gene:PIK3C3 +2.9, gene:ARL8B +1.1, gene:MYO1E +1.3, gene:ITGB5 +1.4), consistent with more lipid-bearing material being routed into the endolysosomal system.", "Step 2 (measured transcripts, inferred compartment expansion): a CLEAR-type lysosomal program is coordinately higher (gene:TFEB +2.4, gene:MITF +1.0; v-ATPase gene:ATP6V1H +6.9, gene:ATP6V1A +4.2, gene:ATP6V0C +3.5 and six further ATP6* subunits; hydrolases gene:GBA +6.7, gene:NAGLU +5.9, gene:HEXA +5.7, gene:SMPD1 +5.6, gene:HEXB +2.2, gene:GLA +1.5, gene:MAN2B1 +1.8, gene:SGSH +1.3, gene:GM2A +2.0, gene:CTSK +7.4, gene:CTSB +5.5, gene:CTSD +2.9), indicating an enlarged acidic degradative compartment handling a glycosphingolipid/membrane-lipid load. This is compartment capacity, not measured hydrolytic flux.", "Step 3 (measured transcripts, inferred sensing state): despite the increased uptake arm, sterol-responsive biosynthesis stays elevated (gene:SREBF2 +1.1, gene:HMGCS1 +1.1, gene:LSS +2.3, gene:DHCR7 +2.7, gene:DHCR24 +3.7, gene:EBP +1.3, gene:ACAT2 +2.0, gene:INSIG1 +1.9, gene:LDLR +1.5) alongside a lipogenic/desaturation arm (gene:SREBF1 +4.7, gene:SCD +4.2, gene:ACSS2 +2.9, gene:FADS1 +1.6, gene:LPCAT1 +3.1, gene:CHPT1 +2.9). Sterol delivered to the cell therefore does not appear to shut off the ER sterol-demand program; the ER-accessible cholesterol pool itself was not measured.", "Step 4 (measured transcripts, inferred routing to storage): esterification and neutral-lipid handling transcripts are higher (gene:SOAT1 +1.3 cholesteryl-ester synthesis, gene:DGAT1 +1.7 triacylglycerol synthesis, gene:MGLL +4.0, gene:FABP3 +1.3, gene:FABP5 +1.1), so incoming and newly synthesized lipid is preferentially channelled into ester/droplet and lysosomal pools rather than to the ER regulatory pool; oxysterol/LXR-type genes are also up (gene:CH25H +1.6, gene:CYP27A1 +1.5, gene:MYLIP +1.3, gene:ABCA7 +2.1, gene:APOE +1.2, gene:SCP2 +5.9), showing the cell simultaneously senses local sterol excess in some compartment while the biosynthetic arm remains on.", "Step 5 (measured transcripts and ambiguous spots, inferred supply): anabolic carbon/reducing-equivalent supply transcripts are higher (gene:MPC2 +8.0, gene:MDH1 +8.7, gene:OGDH +8.6, gene:ACO2 +3.5, gene:ACSS2 +2.9, gene:ATP5ME +5.2, gene:ATP5MC3 +4.7, gene:CYCS +2.6, gene:ETFA +3.5, gene:HADHA +2.9), and the most strongly increased protein spots carry pentose-phosphate/NADPH-pathway candidates among other identities (protein_spot:045 +3.05, protein_spot:046 +2.81, protein_spot:044 +2.38, protein_spot:043 +1.96; candidates include TALDO1 but also ANXA1, ACTB, VPS26A, PSMD7 and others; identity is not resolved). This is compatible with, but does not prove, higher lipogenic flux.", "Step 6 (predicted lipid-level consequence in the supplied mock condition): the loop yields, in APOE4 versus APOE3, a larger lysosomal compartment loaded with glycosphingolipid/sphingomyelin catabolites and a larger esterified neutral-lipid pool (cholesteryl esters, triacylglycerol droplets), with a coexisting activated/lipid-associated microglial surface state (gene:TREM2 +1.3, gene:ITGAX +1.7, gene:CLEC7A +1.5, gene:CD33 +1.8, gene:C1QA +1.2, gene:C1QB +1.1, gene:C1QC +1.2). Whether this state is net-adaptive (higher throughput) or net-sequestering (storage) is decided by flux, not by these abundances."], "assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (all 2212 rows have |effect| \u003e= ~1 in an unspecified log base; 77% are positive). Program directions were therefore judged against this positive-skewed selected-list background, not against 50/50; genes absent from the list (e.g. ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA, PLIN2, HMGCR, FASN) are unknown, not unchanged.", "Program membership was defined a priori from canonical pathway annotation (unverified background knowledge) before looking at signs; members were not dropped to make directions agree. Genes within a program are co-regulated, so coherence is descriptive, not a formal independent-gene enrichment result.", "Transcript abundance is assumed here to track compartment/enzyme capacity, not activity or flux. No hydrolase activity, esterification rate, efflux rate, lipid-droplet content, ER-accessible cholesterol, or protein localization was measured in these data.", "SREBP-target transcript elevation is used as an indirect proxy for a low ER-accessible sterol signal; the regulated step (SREBP cleavage/nuclear entry) was not measured, and SREBF1/SREBF2 transcript increases alone do not establish activation.", "2D-gel protein spots are ambiguous (69 of 92 spots list 5 candidate genes; ACTB, KRT1, KRT10 recur across dozens of spots). Spot effects are used only for compatibility/contradiction, never as confirmation of a named protein; all candidate identities are retained.", "The mechanism describes the ongoing mock state. Any claim about reduced reserve under lipid or myelin challenge is a future-challenge prediction, not an observed defect here.", "Astrocyte co-culture means lipid supply is partly non-cell-autonomous; genotype effects on microglia may be partly astrocyte-mediated, which these data cannot separate.", "Causality is not established by these correlational genotype-difference measurements."], "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective lipid measurement (primary discriminator): in the same mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, lipidomics/imaging should show higher cholesteryl-ester and neutral-lipid-droplet mass and higher lysosomal glycosphingolipid/sphingomyelin catabolite content in APOE4, while the ER-accessible free-cholesterol pool (ALOD4/perfringolysin-O probe or ER-sterol reporter) is NOT higher. If APOE4 shows equal or lower stored ester lipid, or a higher ER-accessible sterol pool despite the elevated SREBP-target transcripts, the routing-to-storage mechanism is weakened.", "Prospective SOAT1 (ACAT1/2) inhibition, e.g. avasimibe, in APOE4 microglia under mock: should lower cholesteryl esters, raise ER-accessible cholesterol, and suppress the SREBP-2 target transcripts (HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, LDLR, INSIG1) toward APOE3 levels. If SREBP-2 targets remain elevated after esterification blockade and free sterol rises, esterification is not the step draining the regulatory pool and the feed-forward step (Step 4) fails.", "Prospective TFEB knockdown/inhibition: if the lysosomal expansion is a compensatory response to lipid load (as claimed), TFEB loss should increase lysosomal lipid storage and worsen droplet accumulation in APOE4 without reducing SREBP-2 target transcripts. If instead TFEB loss reduces lipid storage and normalizes the sterol program, lysosomal expansion is the driver rather than the response, and the ordering of Steps 2-4 is wrong.", "Prospective flux test separating adaptation from sequestration: 13C-acetate (or D2O) tracing plus NBD-cholesterol/BODIPY-myelin pulse-chase should show, in APOE4, higher de novo sterol/fatty-acid synthesis flux together with slower clearance of internalized lipid label from the LAMP1 compartment. Increased synthesis with equal or faster label clearance would support successful high-throughput adaptation instead, and would falsify the sequestering interpretation.", "Prospective challenge (reserve, not baseline): on myelin-debris or apoptotic-cell loading, APOE4 should reach droplet/lysosomal saturation and blunt further uptake sooner than APOE3. A normal APOE4 response to this challenge would show the mock-state differences carry no reduced reserve, weakening the functional significance (though not the descriptive routing claim).", "Negative control from the data: because the selected list contains no interferon or ribosomal program members, the mechanism predicts that unbiased profiling of these same cells shows no coordinated type-I interferon induction in APOE4 under mock; a strong interferon signature would indicate an alternative upstream driver of the lysosomal/lipid changes."]}, "score": {"hypothesis_id": "hyp_041", "cosine_similarity": 0.5238995053055704, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.29374594650006497, "direction_accuracy": 0.6310679611650486, "balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.4638518627921574, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5297508090614887, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"n_features": 618, "cosine_similarity": 0.5238995053055704, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.29374594650006497, "direction_accuracy": 0.6310679611650486, "balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.4638518627921574, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5297508090614887}}}, "cost_usd": 2.08417825, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 5, "global_rank": 7}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b11-hyp_076", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 11, "hypothesis": {"hypothesis_id": "hyp_076", "title": "APOE4 microglia run a storage-routed lipid cycle coupled to expanded lysosomal and nuclear-encoded mitochondrial oxidative machinery, not an interferon/inflammatory program", "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes, day 30) occupy a coordinated high-throughput lipid-handling cell state rather than an inflammatory or interferon-activated one: transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid uptake and for lysosomal hydrolysis and acidification are coherently higher, liberated sterol and fatty acid are routed toward esterification and neutral-lipid storage (SOAT1, DGAT1, AGPAT2, SCD, CIDEB) so that the ER-sensed regulatory sterol pool stays low and SREBP target transcription remains on (SREBF1/2, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, ACAT2, INSIG1, LDLR, SCARB1), and the resulting carbon/reducing-equivalent load is matched by the single most direction-consistent program in the data - mitochondrial substrate carriers, TCA enzymes and every represented nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunit (38/38 up, median +2.64 on the reported log scale, versus a 77% positive selected-list background). The predicted, currently unmeasured consequence is higher cholesteryl-ester/neutral-lipid and lysosomal sphingolipid mass in APOE4 with equal or greater oxidative capacity; no interferon-stimulated-gene module is present, so the assigned inflammation/interferon focus is rejected as the primary mechanism.", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 alters extracellular lipoprotein handling in the microglia-astrocyte co-culture and is accompanied by higher transcripts for lipid and lipoprotein receptors and transfer proteins (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:PLTP +1.06, gene:APOE +1.24; 13/13 represented uptake/storage members positive), which we interpret as increased delivery of lipid to the endolysosomal system (uptake flux itself is not measured).", "The degradative compartment is transcriptionally expanded: gene:TFEB +2.38 with 28/30 represented lysosomal members up, including hydrolases (gene:GAA +10.0, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:CTSK +7.36) and eight v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51), indicating raised capacity for lysosomal lipid/glycosphingolipid catabolism.", "Sterol and fatty acid liberated in that compartment are routed preferentially into esterification and storage rather than into the ER regulatory pool or efflux: gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:CIDEB +1.06, gene:ABHD5 +1.04 (ABCA1/ABCG1 are not represented, so efflux is untested).", "Because the ER-accessible free-sterol pool therefore stays low, SREBP-dependent transcription remains active instead of being switched off by the incoming lipid: gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:INSIG1 +1.87 (an SREBP target) plus gene:LDLR and gene:SCARB1 - a self-sustaining synthesis-plus-uptake-into-storage cycle that increases total cell lipid mass.", "The combined lipolytic and lipogenic flux raises demand for mitochondrial carbon entry, anaplerosis and reoxidation of NADH, and the mitochondrial machinery is coordinately increased: carriers gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50, gene:SLC25A5 +5.56, gene:SLC25A51 +3.72, gene:SLC25A46 +8.77; TCA/anaplerotic enzymes gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:DLD +5.54, gene:IDH3B +2.02, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:GLUD1 +3.17, gene:GLS +1.35 (16/16 up); and all 38 represented nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits (gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:NDUFS7 +5.68, gene:NDUFS8 +4.93, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02, gene:ATP5ME +5.20, gene:COX7A2 +3.36, gene:SDHB +1.65), together with import/chaperone components (gene:TOMM22 +4.63, gene:TIMM44 +2.46, gene:HSPA9 +2.35) and matrix antioxidant transcripts (gene:PRDX3 +3.49, gene:PRDX5 +1.96, gene:GPX4 +2.79).", "This is a maintained metabolic state, not an acute immune activation: the represented NF-kB/chemokine members (gene:CXCL8 +3.11, gene:CXCL16 +3.66, gene:CCL2 +2.12, gene:NFKBIZ +3.07, gene:NLRP3 +1.09, gene:TLR2 +1.20) are 23/27 positive, statistically indistinguishable from the 77% positive selected-list background (binomial p=0.49), the interferon axis is if anything under-represented and mixed (7/13 positive; gene:STAT6 -2.36, gene:STAT5A -2.73, gene:IRF2 -1.17, gene:SOCS4 -1.44, with only gene:IFI27L2 +5.34, gene:IFI16 +1.25, gene:IFNAR1 +1.41 up and no ISG15/MX/OAS/IFIT/HLA/B2M members present in the supplied list), and the pro-resolving gene:ANXA1 +4.15 is up rather than down.", "Downstream, the state predicts a lipid phenotype (higher cholesteryl ester, triacylglycerol/lipid-droplet and lysosomal sphingolipid content in APOE4) with preserved or increased respiratory capacity in the mock condition; the mtDNA-encoded transcript decrease (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33) marks the stoichiometric point at which this expansion could fail under a future energetic or phagocytic challenge, but no failure is demonstrated in the measured condition."], "assumptions": ["Transcript abundance is read as capacity, not as measured flux: uptake rate, lysosomal hydrolase activity, cholesterol-esterification rate, ER free-sterol concentration, lipid-droplet content and respiration were not measured here; every routing and flux statement above is inferred, not observed.", "The RNA rows are two significance-filtered, p-ranked selected lists (1705 up, 507 down, all adjusted p\u003c0.05; log base unspecified and magnitudes up to ~15 are not treated quantitatively), so program coherence is judged against the 77% positive background of that list and absent genes (HMGCR, SQLE, NPC1, ABCA1, ABCG1, PLIN2, STAT1/2, ISG15, MX1, OAS, IFIT, HLA, B2M) are unknown, not unchanged.", "The 2D protein spots carry 2-6 candidate identities each and are dominated by keratin/actin candidates; no spot candidate list contains a nuclear-encoded OXPHOS or TCA protein, so the strongest RNA program has no protein-level test here and no spot is treated as identifying a single protein.", "Causal direction from APOE4 genotype to the lipid-handling state is assumed from the isogenic design, not established; astrocyte co-culture is assumed to be the lipoprotein source and is identical between genotypes.", "The mtDNA-encoded transcript decrease is assumed to be biological rather than a 10X Flex/ambient-RNA or normalization artifact; if it is artifactual, only step 7's challenge caveat is affected, not steps 1-6.", "Effects expected in the supplied mock condition are the storage/synthesis/oxidative-capacity changes; any respiratory or clearance deficit is expected only under a future lipid, phagocytic or energetic challenge and is not claimed for the measured condition."], "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective lipidomics/imaging on the same mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia: APOE4 should show higher cholesteryl ester and triacylglycerol/neutral-lipid-droplet content and higher lysosomal glycosphingolipid and ceramide/sphingomyelin-derived species. If APOE4 neutral lipid and cholesteryl ester are equal to or lower than APOE3, steps 3-4 (storage routing) are wrong.", "Discriminating perturbation: SOAT1/ACAT inhibition (e.g., avasimibe or CI-976) in mock APOE4 microglia should deplete cholesteryl ester, restore the ER-accessible sterol pool and suppress the SREBP target transcripts (HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR24, LDLR, SCARB1) toward APOE3 levels. Persistence of the elevated SREBP program after cholesteryl-ester depletion would falsify the sterol-rerouting step and favour a sterol-sensing-independent transcriptional driver.", "Adaptation versus failed compensation (decisive for the whole claim): extracellular flux analysis should show equal or higher basal, ATP-linked and maximal oxygen consumption and complex I-linked respiration in mock APOE4 despite the lower mtDNA-encoded transcripts. If maximal or complex I-linked respiration is significantly lower in APOE4 while the nuclear OXPHOS transcripts are up, the increased-throughput interpretation is weakened and the competing mito-nuclear stoichiometric-imbalance (failed compensation) mechanism is favoured.", "Substrate tracing: 13C-oleate or 13C-palmitate in mock APOE4 should show increased label incorporation into cholesteryl ester and triacylglycerol and increased 13C enrichment of citrate/glutamate; no genotype difference in either fate would weaken steps 3 and 5.", "Dependence on the expanded degradative arm: TFEB knockdown or lysosomal acid lipase/v-ATPase inhibition should exaggerate lipid-droplet and undigested-lipid accumulation more in APOE4 than in APOE3 (a challenge-revealed reserve deficit, not an ongoing defect). Equal sensitivity of both genotypes would argue the lysosomal expansion is incidental rather than load-driven.", "Negative control for the rejected focus: JAK1/2 inhibition or IFNAR1 blockade in the mock condition should not normalise the mitochondrial, lysosomal or sterol transcript programs; if it does, an interferon-driven mechanism should replace this one."]}, "score": {"hypothesis_id": "hyp_076", "cosine_similarity": 0.5230468470284715, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2691966631336264, "direction_accuracy": 0.4368932038834951, "balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.26418786692759294, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5510388349514563, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"n_features": 618, "cosine_similarity": 0.5230468470284715, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2691966631336264, "direction_accuracy": 0.4368932038834951, "balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.26418786692759294, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5510388349514563}}}, "cost_usd": 2.705538, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 6, "global_rank": 8}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b03-hyp_126", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"hypothesis_id": "hyp_126", "title": "APOE4 microglia run a lipid-uptake plus lysosome-expansion state whose sterol output fails to reach the ER sensor, sustaining SREBP-driven synthesis and storage (routing mismatch, not interferon signaling)", "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 (vs isogenic APOE3) iPSC-derived microglia occupy a coordinated lipid-handling cell state in which transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid capture, endolysosomal delivery and TFEB/MITF-type lysosomal biogenesis are jointly elevated, yet SREBP1/SREBP2 target transcripts remain elevated rather than suppressed; the most parsimonious mechanistic reading is that lysosomally delivered sterol/lipid is preferentially routed into lysosomal and esterified/stored pools instead of the ER regulatory sterol pool, so the ER sensor continues to read 'sterol-poor' while oxysterol/LXR-type outputs rise, producing a futile uptake-plus-synthesis cycle and a lipid-laden lysosomal state with a low-grade chemokine tone. Type I interferon signaling is not supported as the driver and is rejected as the primary explanation. Causality is not established: all evidence is steady-state transcript abundance from a selected differential-expression list plus ambiguous protein spots; no sterol pool, flux, lysosomal pH, hydrolase activity or TFEB localization was measured.", "mechanism_steps": ["STEP 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia show elevated transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid capture and handling receptors and carriers (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:COLEC12 +1.53, gene:STAB1 +1.13, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:PLTP +1.06, gene:ABCA7 +2.14), consistent with (but not proof of) increased lipid influx into the endocytic route.", "STEP 2 (measured abundance, inferred capacity): endolysosomal delivery and a TFEB/MITF-type lysosomal biogenesis program are co-elevated (gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:VPS26A +4.86, gene:SNX3 +3.95, gene:CHMP4B +3.82, gene:DNM2 +5.82; gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03, gene:LAMP1 +1.38, gene:SCARB2 +1.06, gene:CLN3 +1.17, gene:SLC38A7 +7.46, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:CTSD +2.86), i.e. expanded degradative-compartment transcript supply rather than a transcriptional lysosomal deficit.", "STEP 3 (inferred routing, decisive step): despite steps 1-2, ER sterol-sensing output stays in the 'sterol-poor' mode - SREBP factors and their sterol/fatty-acid synthesis targets are up (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:LDLR +1.50), while oxysterol-generating and LXR-type outputs rise in parallel (gene:CH25H +1.62, gene:CYP27A1 +1.49, gene:MYLIP +1.28, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:APOE +1.24). Simultaneous 'need more sterol' and 'sterol present elsewhere' signals indicate compartment mismatch rather than global sterol excess or global sterol shortage.", "STEP 4 (inferred flux/storage): incoming and newly made lipid is biased toward esterified and membrane-storage pools instead of the ER regulatory pool (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:MGLL +4.00, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:LPCAT1 +3.07, gene:CHPT1 +2.91, gene:CIDEB +1.06) with sphingolipid/glycosphingolipid turnover transcripts also raised (gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:GBA2 +2.63, gene:ST3GAL5 +2.17, gene:CERS6 +1.06).", "STEP 5 (predicted state in the measured mock condition): the resulting state is a futile cycle - continued uptake plus continued synthesis into lysosome/droplet pools - so APOE4 microglia should already carry more lysosomal and esterified neutral lipid than APOE3 at day 30, with lysosomal expansion acting as partial, still-incomplete compensation (a defect in ER sterol delivery, not necessarily a defect in bulk hydrolysis).", "STEP 6 (downstream, secondary): the lipid-laden endolysosomal state is accompanied by a modest chemokine/inflammasome-priming tone (gene:CXCL8 +3.11, gene:CXCL1 +1.59, gene:CXCL2 +1.65, gene:CXCL3 +1.56, gene:CCL2 +2.12, gene:NLRP3 +1.09, gene:PYCARD +2.43, gene:IL18 +1.46, gene:MYD88 +2.34, gene:TLR2 +1.20) that is NOT accompanied by a coherent type I interferon program (only gene:IRF8 +1.39, gene:TMEM173 +1.22, gene:CD74 +3.84, gene:CIITA +1.50 represented; gene:IRF2 -1.17; no ISG15/MX/OAS/IFIT/STAT1/STAT2/IRF7/GBP rows supplied), so interferon signaling is rejected as the driver and the chemokine tone is placed downstream, not upstream."], "assumptions": ["The 2212 supplied RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05; 77.1% positive), so program coherence was judged against that biased background, not against 50/50; genes absent from the list (e.g. NPC1, ABCA1, HMGCR, SQLE, MCOLN1, TNF, IL1B, STAT1, MX1) are unknown, not unchanged.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and effect magnitudes are unusually large; only signs and relative ranks are treated as informative, and no cross-modality magnitude comparison with the log2 protein spots is made.", "Marker membership was pre-specified from canonical pathway knowledge (unverified background knowledge; literature/database retrieval was disabled) and queried before effects were read; represented-vs-queried counts are reported and no member was dropped to make directions agree.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to correlate with, but not to demonstrate, protein level, enzymatic activity, TFEB nuclear localization, lysosomal acidification or lipid flux; every activity, routing and flux statement is inferred, not observed.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate (3-6 candidate genes each; ACTB appears in 26 spots), so no spot is treated as identifying an individual protein; spots are used only for compatibility/contradiction.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies exogenous lipoproteins, so a lipid-uptake-driven state is plausible in this specific culture; the mechanism is stated for the mock (unchallenged) condition, and any additional fragility under lipid or inflammatory challenge is a predicted future-challenge phenotype, not an observed one."], "falsifiable_predictions": ["PROSPECTIVE DISCRIMINATOR (routing mismatch vs matched high throughput): acute sterol loading of mock APOE4 and APOE3 microglia (LDL or cholesterol/methyl-beta-cyclodextrin, 4-8 h) should suppress SREBP2 targets (HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, LDLR) markedly less in APOE4 than in APOE3, while total and lysosomal cholesterol rises at least as much in APOE4. If APOE4 shows normal or stronger SREBP2 feedback suppression, the routing-mismatch step (STEP 3) is falsified and 'successful high-throughput adaptation' is favored.", "PROSPECTIVE: filipin/LipidTOX plus LAMP1 imaging and lipidomics in mock day-30 APOE4 vs APOE3 should show increased lysosomal free cholesterol, cholesteryl ester and glycosphingolipid content with equal-or-greater LAMP1+ compartment volume. Absence of lipid accumulation despite the transcript pattern would weaken the whole mechanism.", "PROSPECTIVE RESCUE: relieving lysosomal sterol export (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin) or blocking esterification (SOAT1/ACAT inhibitor, e.g. avasimibe) should lower SREBP2-target transcripts and reduce the chemokine tone (CXCL8, CCL2) in APOE4 toward APOE3 without lowering LAMP1/hydrolase transcripts first. No normalization of SREBP2 targets would weaken STEP 3-4.", "PROSPECTIVE ACTIVITY TEST: per-cell GBA, HEXA and GAA enzymatic activity and BODIPY-LDL degradation rate should be equal or higher in APOE4 (expanded capacity), while an ER-targeted sterol biosensor reads lower in APOE4. Finding reduced hydrolase activity instead would replace 'routing mismatch' with a genuine lysosomal catabolic deficit.", "PROSPECTIVE NEGATIVE CONTROL for the rejected focus: JAK1/2 inhibition or IFNAR blockade in mock culture should leave the lysosomal, SREBP and lipid-storage transcript differences essentially intact. If JAK/IFNAR blockade abolishes them, an interferon-driven explanation would supersede this mechanism.", "PROSPECTIVE (protein level, spot ambiguity resolved): targeted immunoblot/MS of CTSB, CTSD, HEXB and ATP6V1E1 should show APOE4 increases consistent with the transcripts; persistent decreases (as some spots such as protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:064 would allow) would indicate post-transcriptional loss of lysosomal protein and weaken STEP 2."]}, "score": {"hypothesis_id": "hyp_126", "cosine_similarity": 0.5224560945546165, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2870096593090623, "direction_accuracy": 0.5792880258899676, "balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.43254070819333157, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5185728155339806, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"n_features": 618, "cosine_similarity": 0.5224560945546165, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2870096593090623, "direction_accuracy": 0.5792880258899676, "balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.43254070819333157, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5185728155339806}}}, "cost_usd": 2.0461345, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 7, "global_rank": 9}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b08-hyp_145", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 8, "hypothesis": {"hypothesis_id": "hyp_145", "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a sterol-routing state: lipid is diverted into lysosomal and esterified pools, so ER sterol sensing stays 'low' and uptake, synthesis and lysosome/ER-Golgi biogenesis run together", "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes) differ from APOE3 not by an unfolded-protein/ER-proteostasis stress response but by a coordinated lipid-handling cell state: transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid uptake (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:APOE +1.24), for ER-localised esterification/storage (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SCD +4.17) and for SREBP-driven de novo sterol/fatty-acid synthesis (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:INSIG1 +1.87) are simultaneously higher, together with a TFEB/MITF-associated lysosomal-hydrolase program (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03, gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23) and increased ER-to-Golgi glycoprotein-production machinery (gene:MLEC +10.21, gene:DDOST +6.22, gene:STT3A +3.39, gene:RPN1 +1.06, gene:COPA +4.27, gene:COPE +4.33, gene:GOLPH3 +3.68, gene:GNPTG +3.02, gene:IGF2R +2.02). Co-elevation of uptake and of sterol synthesis is the informative pattern: it is the signature expected when incoming sterol is routed away from the ER regulatory (accessible) pool into cholesteryl-ester/neutral-lipid and lysosomal membrane pools, so SCAP/INSIG-SREBP continues to report sterol insufficiency while total cell lipid rises. We claim an altered routing/cell state, not a demonstrated degradative bottleneck; degradative flux was not measured.", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia express higher transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid capture and its receptors (gene:SCARB1, gene:LDLR, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE, gene:ABCA7) and for phagocytic/DAM-like surface machinery (gene:ITGAX +1.69, gene:CLEC7A +1.46, gene:MERTK +1.30, gene:GPNMB +1.11, gene:C1QA +1.25), consistent with increased delivery of lipoprotein- and membrane-derived lipid to the endolysosome (inferred flux, not measured).", "Step 2 (inferred routing): sterol arriving at the ER is preferentially esterified and stored rather than retained in the ER accessible pool, supported by higher gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1 and the monounsaturated-FA supply enzyme gene:SCD that favours cholesteryl-ester/TAG droplet formation; gene:CH25H (+1.62) indicates active oxysterol handling.", "Step 3 (sensing consequence): with the ER regulatory sterol pool held low, SCAP-SREBP2/SREBP1 processing stays permissive, sustaining gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:ACAT2 and gene:LDLR while gene:INSIG1 (itself an SREBP target) also rises - a feed-forward loop in which synthesis and uptake are not switched off by the enlarging stored lipid pool.", "Step 4 (compartment expansion): the lipid load, plus TFEB/MITF-associated transcription (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF), expands the acid-hydrolase and v-ATPase program (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:LAMP1 +1.38, gene:SCARB2 +1.06, gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:NPC2 +1.17, gene:SLC38A7 +7.46).", "Step 5 (secretory support, not stress): because hydrolases are N-glycosylated, M6P-tagged cargo, the expanded lysosomal program is accompanied by higher ER OST/glycan-QC and early secretory transcripts (gene:MLEC, gene:DDOST, gene:STT3A, gene:STT3B +1.40, gene:RPN1, gene:MCFD2 +3.00, gene:COPA, gene:COPE, gene:COPB1 +1.04, gene:RAB1B +1.67, gene:RAB6A +1.23, gene:GOLPH3, gene:TRAPPC3 +2.47, gene:GNPTG, gene:IGF2R). This is biosynthetic-load matching; it is not a canonical UPR (see assumptions).", "Step 6 (energetic coupling): nuclear-encoded oxidative/anaplerotic transcripts rise coherently (gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:DLD +5.54, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:SLC25A5 +5.56, gene:ATP5F1B +2.65, gene:NDUFA8 +3.05, gene:COX5B +2.33, gene:PRDX3 +3.49, gene:GPX4 +2.79), consistent with an ATP/redox-supported high-turnover lipid-processing state rather than a collapsed one.", "Step 7 (predicted lipid phenotype in the measured mock condition): the net output of steps 1-4 is a shifted lipid distribution - more cholesteryl ester and neutral-lipid/droplet lipid and more lysosomal sphingolipid/glycolipid intermediates per cell in APOE4 - while free (ER-accessible) cholesterol is not correspondingly raised."], "assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected significant differential-expression list (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05; 1705/2212 = 77% positive), so upward direction alone is weakly informative; the argument rests on high representation of lysosomal (31/33 represented members positive), sterol/lipid (21/21) and nuclear-OXPHOS (28/28) members plus the specific co-occurrence of uptake with synthesis, not on a 50/50 sign expectation. Genes are not independent; this is descriptive coherence, not a formal enrichment test.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified in the source; effects are kept on the reported scale and are not converted or compared quantitatively with the protein spots' log2 fold changes.", "Genes absent from the list (e.g. HSPA5, XBP1, ATF4, HERPUD1, CALR, CANX, HSP90B1, ERN1, HMGCR, SQLE, NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, PLIN2) are unknown, not unchanged; the UPR argument below is therefore an argument from what was selected, not proof of absence.", "The assigned ER-proteostasis/UPR focus is rejected as the primary mechanism: the represented UPR set is 12 up / 4 down (median +1.97), statistically indistinguishable from the 77%-up background (binomial p ~ 0.70), the ERAD recognition/dislocation arm is down (gene:SEL1L -2.09, gene:EDEM1 -1.37, gene:DERL1 -1.19, gene:PDIA3 -1.26), and the three spots whose candidate lists include the ER lumenal chaperones HSP90B1/HSPA5 (protein_spot:001 -0.485, protein_spot:004 -0.678, protein_spot:005 -0.138) are all non-significant and negative. Elevated gene:ATF6 and gene:DDIT3 transcripts do not establish ATF6 cleavage or an integrated stress response; only the secretory/glycosylation arm of the focus is retained, as biosynthetic load matching.", "Protein spots are ambiguous (69/92 carry 5 candidate identities; KRT1/KRT10/ACTB dominate the candidate frequency), so no spot is treated as confirming an individual protein. Spots containing hydrolase candidates go in both directions (protein_spot:053 +1.54 with CTSD among candidates; protein_spot:058 -0.85, protein_spot:067 -1.00, protein_spot:069 -1.38 with CTSD/CTSB/HEXB among candidates), which is compatible with altered proteolytic processing or with resolution limits and cannot adjudicate hydrolase protein levels.", "All measurements are steady-state abundance. Uptake rate, esterification flux, lysosomal degradative flux, SREBP cleavage, ER accessible-cholesterol concentration and subcellular localisation were not measured and are inferred.", "The condition is mock (unchallenged). The mechanism asserts an ongoing routing difference in this condition; any reduced capacity to handle an acute lipid or myelin load would be a reserve deficit revealed only by a future challenge and is not claimed as an established defect here.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies lipoproteins, so uptake-driven routing is possible in the measured system; genotype-driven differences in astrocyte-derived ligand were not measured.", "Causality is not established: this is a hypothesis consistent with cross-sectional isogenic abundance differences."], "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective lipid measurement in the same mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia: cholesteryl esters and triacylglycerol/neutral-lipid content per cell should be higher in APOE4 with an increased CE:free-cholesterol ratio, and lysosomal sphingolipid/glycosphingolipid substrates (e.g. sphingomyelin, hexosylceramide) should also rise. If total cholesteryl ester and neutral lipid are unchanged or lower in APOE4 while sterol-synthesis transcripts remain elevated, the routing claim fails and simple increased synthesis/export becomes the better model.", "Discriminating perturbation (prospective): SOAT1/ACAT inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) in APOE4 microglia should raise the ER-accessible cholesterol pool and thereby suppress SREBP-2 target transcripts (HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, LDLR) toward APOE3 levels while lowering cholesteryl esters. If SREBP-2 targets stay elevated after esterification is blocked and free cholesterol rises, the proposed ER-sensing-pool depletion step is wrong.", "Direct sensing test (prospective): an ER accessible-cholesterol probe (e.g. ALOD4) should report equal or lower ER accessible cholesterol in APOE4 despite higher total cholesterol; finding higher ER accessible cholesterol in APOE4 together with elevated SREBP targets would contradict the mechanism and instead indicate SCAP/INSIG sensing failure or SREBP-independent transcriptional drive.", "Adaptation versus failed compensation (prospective): pulse-chase of fluorescent lipoprotein/myelin cargo with DQ-BSA and BODIPY-cholesterol should show equal or faster degradative and esterification throughput in APOE4 in the mock state if this is successful high-throughput adaptation; slower cargo clearance with the same expanded hydrolase transcript program would reclassify the state as failed compensation (a lysosomal bottleneck) and would require revising steps 3-4, though the routing prediction on CE could still hold.", "TFEB dependence (prospective): TFEB/MITF knockdown in APOE4 microglia should reduce the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript program and the ER/Golgi glycoprotein-machinery transcripts (DDOST, STT3A, GNPTG) coordinately, and increase undegraded lysosomal lipid; if hydrolase transcripts fall but the ER/Golgi machinery transcripts do not, step 5 (load matching) is weakened.", "Challenge-only prediction, explicitly not claimed for the measured condition: after an acute myelin or oxidised-LDL load, APOE4 microglia should show disproportionate droplet accumulation and blunted further induction of sterol-synthesis genes relative to APOE3; equal handling under load would show that the mock-state routing difference carries no reduced reserve."]}, "score": {"hypothesis_id": "hyp_145", "cosine_similarity": 0.5214928384904949, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2343526193433554, "direction_accuracy": 0.6262135922330098, "balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3776908023483366, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5177443365695793, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"n_features": 618, "cosine_similarity": 0.5214928384904949, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2343526193433554, "direction_accuracy": 0.6262135922330098, "balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3776908023483366, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5177443365695793}}}, "cost_usd": 2.034263, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 8, "global_rank": 10}], "selection": {"top_n": 10, "metric": "cosine_similarity", "evaluated_count": 2498}, "note": "Previously inspected development panel. Scores rank hypothesis-predictor pairs, not causal validity. Astra and Claude use different predictors and harnesses. Ongoing batches are excluded from this fixed snapshot.", "snapshot_at": "2026-09-10T12:45:52.373420+00:00", "snapshot_note": "Fixed snapshot: 1,432 historical pairs + 967 new Opus + 99 Astra max. New Opus exclusions: 5 failed, 4 interrupted, 24 unstarted; Astra: 1 initial failed attempt. The newer running Astra batch is excluded.", "chart_caption": "Chart: evidence-v2 Opus (1,325), Astra max (99), and Astra xhigh (38) only; the table and top ten also include original-prompt and Sonnet cohorts. Dots show the mean best cosine over uniform random subsets. Bars are central 95% subset-maximum ranges, not confidence intervals or biological uncertainty. Two agent sessions per valid pair; failed attempts and internal turns are excluded. Predictors and harnesses differ. Sonnet cohort means retain legacy zero scores for mathematically undefined zero-norm cosines; these cannot enter the top ten."};
